<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>Today skyBlip Go. Next, ADS-B on board.</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">
    skyBlip Go and Go+ are available. The skyBlip Bravo firmware is in
    development, for an X1 you can buy today. The Panel and the skyPost
    stations are in design, on the same code base.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">In the aircraft</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    skyBlip Go receives ADS-L and FLARM. It does not receive ADS-B on
    1090&nbsp;MHz, which airliners, business jets, helicopters and many touring
    aircraft transmit. skyBlip Bravo will receive it in the aircraft, with no
    ground station.
  </p>

  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3 id="bravo">skyBlip Bravo.</h3>
      <p>The ADS-B receiver, for your phone or your Go. The hardware, a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, is on sale. The skyBlip Bravo firmware is in development.</p>
      <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "skyBlip Bravo" %></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 id="tango">skyBlip Tango.</h3>
      <p>A Go paired with a Bravo: ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM on the Go&rsquo;s radar, and your position in ADS-L. A Go+ and a Bravo make a Tango+.</p>
      <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "skyBlip Tango" %></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For glass cockpits</p>
      <h3>skyBlip <span class="highlight">Panel</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        A fixed box behind the instrument panel, powered by the aircraft. No
        screen: the traffic shows on the panel display, Garmin G3X, Dynon
        SkyView and the others, like a factory traffic source.
      </p>
      <p>
        ADS-L transmit and receive. RS-232 outputs (FLARM NMEA or GDL90) to the
        EFIS, GDL90 over Wi-Fi, FLARM NMEA over Bluetooth.
      </p>
      <p class="feature-guide"><small>Hardware: LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, MAX3232 RS-232 adapter.</small></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot shot--photo">
      <%= pages_image_tag "skyblip-panel-board.avif", alt: "skyBlip Panel: the board in its case, with its antenna" %>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Around the airfield, a skyPost station will receive ADS-B, add the traffic
    of the Open Glider Network and the weather (QNH, METAR, TAF), and relay it
    all in ADS-L to every skyBlip Go in range.
  </p>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Helio.</h3>
      <p>The solar station. Self-powered, in a weatherproof case on a mast. Will receive ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, Ebyte E80-900MBL 1090 receiver, LilyGO T-Solar kit.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Bridge.</h3>
      <p>For existing stations: OGN, PiAware, adsb.lol. Will relay in ADS-L the traffic they already decode, without touching their feeds.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%= render "shared/cta" %>
</section>
